Z||000000||Oreif||01-31-2001||11:19 AM||||I read a magazine that said the word <I> merde </I> was pronounced <I> emm erre duex </I> in French. Is this correct? What does the word mean?  (yes it was in an article talking about MR2's.)||||reg||5
Z||000001||p4n1c||01-31-2001||11:21 AM||||merde = sh** <P>(<B>edit:</B> it's actually stink, but it's also used for slang, crap or sh**).<P>And that is the proper pronounceation that they gave.  Goes along with j'ai cheia(more than likely spelled wrong) ma pantelon.  Or I sh** my pants in english.  I learned that from a friend that speaks french.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm not french BTW.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The misconception is that all Canadians speak and are French.  Not true.  Mostly only Quebec with scatterings in other provinces, or just people that took french in school.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||01-31-2001||02:44 PM||||ahahaha.. Assuming that all Canadians speak french is almost as big a stereotype as all americans have a rusty Camaro on their front yard (everyone does, right?). Alas, I do speak french.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||RiceCooker||01-31-2001||03:46 PM||||Je'mappelle RiceCooker.<P>I hate french. Just because our country is bilingual (The Quebecers always complain and want to seperate anyways) I had to take French classes in school and everything from Road signs to cereal boxes has to be in both languages. It's a sensitive subject for many people but know, we don't all speak french.||||reg||1
